    "description": "The source implements Ack(m,n) with the direct recurrence A(0,n)=n+1, A(m,0)=A(m-1,1), and A(m,n)=A(m-1,A(m,n-1)). Its main fixes m=3 and reads n from argv, defaulting to 8 when the launcher supplies no option; this yields A(3,8)=2045. The suite exposes the same recurrence over a bounded pair of inputs, with 0<=m<=3 and 0<=n<=8. Each benchmark repetition makes one function call because recursive work grows rapidly.",
